ts so essentially we  have multiple instances of this  architecture running across GCP estate  so why do we do it why do we why do we  have this single tenant deployment model  previously when we run everything on  premises in our own data center we  didn't have a single tenant deployment  model we had very big clusters and we  shared them between multiple clients now  we're in the cloud we can we can use a  single tenant deployment model and the  reason really is it's one of segregation  again really it's keeping things  separate that don't need to be in the  same place it's a lot simpler for us to  assign access for clients to actually  access our infrastructure we can just we  can control that with the natural  boundary that a GCP project provides  it's a lot simpler for us to operate we  don't need to worry about using Kerberos  or anything like that cost transparency  is a big factor for us if we want to  actually see the cost of serving a  particular clients it's very easy to do  that because the billing data is all  kanabi group talk to a particular  project or a couple of projects so we  can see very easily the cost of actually  serving a client and you saw that on on  an earlier slide the other big advantage  that it provides is the ability to scale  from zero so what do I mean by that if  you think about how we work we we will  sign a client to do some work from them  we provision to two projects on their  behalf at that point it's essentially  nothing in those projects there's no  data  there's no runtime components and not  none of our data scientists or our data  engineers will actually have access to  it so literally we start we have nothing  it makes it a lot easier to scale that  up as than when we need we never had the  capability to do that when we were on  premises because we were using share  clusters so we had to provision massive  clusters in advance of actually signing  our clients before we actually know that  we were going to have them so ma